course: dictionary
lesson: 6320
title: Moth: a word with clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A moth is an insect with four wings, like a butterfly. Most moths have dull brown or grey wings, not bright colours. When you meet an unknown word, look at the words around it, because they give you clues.
explain: «Moths live in it, so a still, greenish sloth is hard to spot among the leaves.» The sloth's fur is a hiding place for moths, so a moth must be a small creature that lives in fur. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words appear in phrases. «Like a moth to a flame» means someone is pulled towards something that could harm them. Once you know the basic meaning, a phrase is much easier to understand.
fact: A moth is an insect with four wings, and most moths have dull brown or grey wings.
fact: Most moths fly at night, and many are drawn to lights.
fact: A moth's life cycle has four stages: egg, caterpillar, pupa (cocoon), then adult.
fact: Some moths' young (larvae) eat holes in wool clothes, which is why a jumper can be «moth-eaten».
fact: Many moths feed on nectar, and this helps them act as pollinators.
exercise: «Moths live in it, so a still, greenish sloth is hard to spot among the leaves.» What is a moth in this sentence? | A kind of green leaf | A large animal that lives in the trees | A type of river fish | *A small insect that lives in fur
exercise: «Like a moth to a flame» suggests what? | Someone is cold and needs a fire | Someone is very fast and can fly | *Someone is drawn to something that could harm them | Someone is hiding in the dark
exercise: Which fact about moths is true? | Moths have six wings | Moths are never drawn to lights | Moths only fly in the daytime | *Most moths fly at night
test: Most moths have dull brown or grey wings. What colour are most moths' wings? | Gold | Bright red | Bright blue | *Dull brown or grey
test: What is the correct order of a moth's life cycle? | Adult, egg, pupa, caterpillar | *Egg, caterpillar, pupa, adult | Pupa, adult, egg, caterpillar | Caterpillar, egg, adult, pupa
exam: «The silk moth cannot fly properly and is not found anywhere in the wild.» What does this sentence suggest about the silk moth? | It is found in every garden | *People have changed it so much that it depends on them | It lives only in the sea | It flies faster than any bird
